      "source": [
        "# Creating Visualizations for Data Analysis\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "3b76da23-a998-4b58-816c-334a675aebe8"
      },
      "source": [
        "### TASK 1.1: Develop a *Line chart* using the functionality of pandas to show how Average automobile sales fluctuate from year to year\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "5562d273-52ae-4bc1-96fb-f69f22bca463"
      },
      "source": [
        "<details><summary>Click here for a hint</summary>\n",
        "\n",
        "<p>\n",
        "You will require:-\n",
        "<br>to group the year and calculate the average on the 'Automobile Sales', as the data has years and months column\n",
        "<br>make use of .plot() with kind = 'line'\n",
        "<br>donot forget to include labels and title\n",
        "</details>\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 470
        },
        "id": "2ec53e34-072e-4956-92d9-09d67a292150",
        "outputId": "a98b9c26-48e2-4d53-8c88-52a4393f02cb"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "display_data",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": [
              "<Figure size 1000x600 with 1 Axes>"
            ],
            "image/png": "\n"
          },
          "metadata": {}
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "    #create data for plotting\n",
        "    df_line = df.groupby(df['Year'])['Automobile_Sales'].mean()\n",
        "    #create figure\n",
        "    plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\n",
        "    df_line.plot(kind = 'line')\n",
        "    plt.xlabel('Year')\n",
        "    plt.ylabel('Automobile Sales')\n",
        "    plt.title('Average Automobile Sales Fluctuation from Year to Year')\n",
        "    plt.show()"
      ],
      "execution_count": 12
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "227ea956-2b4d-4941-ad5b-32cec415f84a"
      },
      "source": [
        "### Include the following on the plot\n",
        "ticks on x- axis with all the years, to identify the years of recession\n",
        "<br>annotation for at least two years of recession\n",
        "<br>Title as Automobile Sales during Recession\n",
        "<br>\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "bbab15ff-db36-4cbb-a756-00e1873387f9"
      },
      "source": [
        "<details><summary>Click here for a hint</summary>\n",
        "    <p>\n",
        "    You can create the list for the range 1980 till 2023 and pass that list to the plt.xticks function or you can directly pass the range to the function.\n",
        "    You might need to rotate the ticks to an angle so that they fit in well on the axis\n",
        "    You can include annotation with plt.text(x, y, 'text to display')\n",
        "    </p>\n",
        "</details>\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 489
        },
        "id": "b2a7c180-10b0-47ce-b779-8991d45f3d6e",
        "outputId": "26c2def8-6f37-4cba-87e3-73a24881d303"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "display_data",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": [
              "<Figure size 1000x600 with 1 Axes>"
            ],
            "image/png": "\n"
          },
          "metadata": {}
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\n",
        "df_line = df.groupby(df['Year'])['Automobile_Sales'].mean()\n",
        "df_line.plot(kind = 'line')\n",
        "plt.xticks(list(range(1980,2024)), rotation = 75)\n",
        "plt.xlabel('Year')\n",
        "plt.ylabel('Automobile Sales Volume')\n",
        "plt.title('Automobile Sales during Recession')\n",
        "plt.text(1982, 650, '1981-82 Recession')\n",
        "plt.text(2008, 650, '2007-2008 Recession')\n",
        "plt.legend()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "execution_count": 13
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "73470905-cfb1-4a8b-a162-7954007fa660"
      },
      "source": [
        "---\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "afcabd08-181a-40e8-a4af-41d4b7b1b2ec"
      },
      "source": [
        "\n",
        "####  TASK 1.2: How do trends in advertising expenditure correlate with automobile sales during non-recession periods, and what insights can be derived from this relationship.\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 370
        },
        "id": "9c07b47c-cfd0-4bf5-9fbd-67bb70ee602a",
        "outputId": "d2c18491-aba3-4062-fe68-06f4009a8281"
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "display_data",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": [
              "<Figure size 1200x600 with 1 Axes>"
            ],
            "image/png": "\n"
          },
          "metadata": {}
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "# Assuming 'df' is your dataset\n",
        "df_non_rec = df[df['Recession'] == 0]\n",
        "\n",
        "# Calculate average automobile sales and average advertising expenditure by year (non-recession)\n",
        "df_trends = df_non_rec.groupby('Year', as_index=False).agg(\n",
        "    Avg_Sales=('Automobile_Sales', 'mean'),\n",
        "    Avg_Ad_Spend=('Advertising_Expenditure', 'mean')\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "# Create line plots for average sales and advertising expenditure over the years\n",
        "plt.figure(figsize=(12, 6))\n",
        "sns.lineplot(data=df_trends, x='Year', y='Avg_Sales', marker='o', linestyle='-', color='green', label='Average Sales')\n",
        "sns.lineplot(data=df_trends, x='Year', y='Avg_Ad_Spend', marker='s', linestyle='--', color='blue', label='Average Ad Spend')\n",
        "\n",
        "# Add labels, legend, title, and grid\n",
        "plt.xlabel('Year')\n",
        "plt.ylabel('Value')\n",
        "plt.title('Advertising Expenditure and Automobile Sales during non Recession Periods')\n",
        "plt.legend()\n",
        "plt.grid(axis='y', linestyle='--', alpha=0.7)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Show the plot\n",
        "plt.tight_layout()\n",
        "plt.show()"
      ],
      "execution_count": 14
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "af4ab1b4-2bd2-470e-a86c-5b7dc4426975"
      },
      "source": [
        "#### From the above plot, what insights have you gained?<br> Type in your answer below:\n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### **Inference & Insights from the Advertising vs. Sales Plot (Non-Recession Periods)**\n",
        "\n",
        "1. **Sales_Volatility** : Automobile sales fluctuate significantly year-over-year, whereas advertising expenditure is much more consistent and exhibits lower variance.<br>\n",
        "2. **Independent Spikes**: Significant peaks in vehicle sales (for instance, around the mid-1990s and late-2010s) do not strictly correspond to elevated advertising expenditure. This suggests that during stable (non-recession) economic climates, consumer demand is driven strongly by market dynamics, vehicle pricing, and external financial factors rather than being directly proportional to ad spend.<br>\n",
        "3. **Baseline Advertising**: The steady baseline of advertising suggests that the company maintains its brand presence and market share continuously, while sales are left to respond to organic consumer demand cycles.<br>"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "p9teAnhG3nvY"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "96474322-81d2-4a9a-b3cd-3a150e6917dd"
      },
      "source": [
        "<details>\n",
